    "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Transportation_Problem\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 300)  # Set time limit to 300 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    sources = list(range(7))  # S0..S6\n    destinations = list(range(6))  # D0..D5\n\n    supplies = [94, 47, 50, 55, 67, 37, 69]\n    demands = [14, 47, 21, 70, 72, 58]\n\n    # Cost matrix: rows correspond to sources S0..S6, columns to destinations D0..D5\n    costs = [\n        [ 12.02,   7.06,  16.65,  18.43,  14.67,   8.11],  # S0\n        [ 23.82,  25.36,  18.15,  24.40,   5.59,  28.53],  # S1\n        [ 23.97,  24.46,   7.90,  18.60,  26.82,   7.64],  # S2\n        [ 12.12,  15.71,  26.28,  18.18,  23.66,  22.78],  # S3\n        [ 24.61,  19.52,   5.23,  16.70,  13.98,  10.76],  # S4\n        [ 10.46,  27.17,  16.21,  15.54,   6.49,   6.83],  # S5\n        [  9.72,  22.59,  18.27,   9.91,  21.22,  24.25],  # S6\n    ]\n\n    # Decision variables:\n    # Flow_S{i}_D{j} >= 0 is the quantity shipped from source i to destination j\n    flows = {}\n    for i in sources:\n        for j in destinations:\n            flows[(i, j)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_S{i}_D{j}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total transportation cost\n    m.setObjective(\n        quicksum(costs[i][j] * flows[(i, j)] for i in sources for j in destinations),\n        GRB.MINIMIZE\n    )\n\n    # Supply constraints: Shipments from each source <= its supply\n    for i in sources:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for j in destinations) <= supplies[i],\n            name=f\"Supply_S{i}\"\n        )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Shipments to each destination >= its demand\n    for j in destinations:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(flows[(i, j)] for i in sources) >= demands[j],\n            name=f\"Demand_D{j}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "To: Executive Leadership and Regional Operations\nFrom: Supply Chain Director\nDate: [Insert Date]\nSubject: Cost-effective multi-source shipping plan to meet all destination requirements\n\nSituation:\nWe operate multiple warehouses and factories supplying a network of stores, customers, and regional hubs. Transportation spend is a major component of our cost to serve, and on-time, in-full delivery is central to customer satisfaction. Aligning available inventory at sources with required quantities at destinations\u2014while considering route-by-route shipping costs\u2014is essential to protect margins and service.\n\nProblem:\nWe need a clear, lane-level shipping plan that specifies how much to move from each source to each destination so that:\n- No source ships more than the inventory or capacity it has available.\n- Every destination receives the full quantity required.\n- Total transportation spend is kept as low as possible.\nPartial shipments are allowed, so a destination\u2019s requirement may be fulfilled from more than one source when this reduces cost or mitigates risk.\n\nApproach:\n- Confirm the latest available inventory or capacity at each source, the required quantities at each destination, and the per-unit cost to ship on each route.\n- Use these inputs to produce a recommended plan that assigns shipment quantities to each source\u2013destination lane, ensuring all needs are met without exceeding availability.\n- Validate operational feasibility with distribution and carrier teams, then publish the plan and expected transportation spend for the planning horizon.\n\nWhy this matters:\n- Reduces overall transportation costs by selecting the most economical lanes.\n- Improves service reliability by ensuring every destination is fully supplied.\n- Minimizes expedites and last-minute rebalancing by proactively aligning supply and demand.\n\nNext steps:\n- Confirm the data in the annex.\n- Generate the recommended shipping plan and review with operations.\n- Execute the plan and monitor performance, refreshing as data changes.\n\nAnnex \u2013 Shipping Data:\n[94, 47, 50, 55, 67, 37, 69]\n[14, 47, 21, 70, 72, 58]\nCost Matrix (7 sources \u00d7 6 destinations):\n\nSource\\Dest | D 0 | D 1 | D 2 | D 3 | D 4 | D 5\n-----------------------------------------------\nS 0        |  12.02 |   7.06 |  16.65 |  18.43 |  14.67 |   8.11\nS 1        |  23.82 |  25.36 |  18.15 |  24.40 |   5.59 |  28.53\nS 2        |  23.97 |  24.46 |   7.90 |  18.60 |  26.82 |   7.64\nS 3        |  12.12 |  15.71 |  26.28 |  18.18 |  23.66 |  22.78\nS 4        |  24.61 |  19.52 |   5.23 |  16.70 |  13.98 |  10.76\nS 5        |  10.46 |  27.17 |  16.21 |  15.54 |   6.49 |   6.83\nS 6        |   9.72 |  22.59 |  18.27 |   9.91 |  21.22 |  24.25",
